      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Question",
        "Answer"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Is Homer one poet or many?",
          "Oral-formulaic theory makes the question wrong — each performance is a re-composition"
        ],
        [
          "Is an oral tradition accurate?",
          "Stable structure, variable surface — facts drift, schema persists"
        ],
        [
          "Can oral cultures have complex thought?",
          "Yes — Goody overreached; oral cultures have sophisticated logic in situational form"
        ],
        [
          "What is a formula?",
          "Metrically fitting phrase reused across performances (not a cliché — functional unit)"
        ],
        [
          "What's the difference between myth and legend?",
          "Myth: sacred, cosmological, set in other time/world; Legend: believed true, set in recent/here"
        ],
        [
          "What distinguishes oral history from oral tradition?",
          "Oral history: recorded living memory (methodological); tradition: multi-generational transmission"
        ]
      ]
    },
